WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.414 --> 00:00:01.863
(Static)

00:00:01.863 --> 00:00:03.012
- Wow!

00:00:03.012 --> 00:00:03.845
- Wow.

00:00:04.681 --> 00:00:05.514
(screams)

00:00:05.514 --> 00:00:08.692
(lively music)

00:00:08.692 --> 00:00:11.110
- Hi, my name is Tom
and I am a copywriter.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.280
I write commercials.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:13.735
- I'm Kevin Weir,

00:00:13.735 --> 00:00:16.660
I'm the creative director
at Droga5 in New York.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:17.602
- Hey, I'm Leigh.

00:00:17.602 --> 00:00:20.795
- I'm Barrett. We have done
four superbowl commercials.

00:00:20.795 --> 00:00:21.628
- That's right.

00:00:21.628 --> 00:00:22.832
- Hopefully we can give
your some good advice.

00:00:22.832 --> 00:00:24.715
- Just buying the space in the

00:00:24.715 --> 00:00:26.498
Super Bowl is 4 million dollars.

00:00:26.498 --> 00:00:30.255
- There is extra pressure
to make it entertaining.

00:00:30.255 --> 00:00:32.151
- You look at it as like,
okay we have a captive

00:00:32.151 --> 00:00:34.575
audience of hundreds
of millions of people.

00:00:34.575 --> 00:00:36.425
What is the craziest thing that we can do

00:00:36.425 --> 00:00:38.179
just to get people talking?

00:00:38.179 --> 00:00:40.617
- When the general public
is judging your work

00:00:40.617 --> 00:00:42.828
and not just advertising people.

00:00:42.828 --> 00:00:44.757
- (interviewer) This is
the people's commercial?

00:00:44.757 --> 00:00:45.628
- Yes, exactly.

00:00:45.628 --> 00:00:47.522
- (interviewer) Three
ingredients to be an awesome

00:00:47.522 --> 00:00:49.664
Super Bowl commercial, what are they?

00:00:49.664 --> 00:00:50.714
- It's got to be original.

00:00:50.714 --> 00:00:53.610
Super Bowls, they always have celebrities

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:54.443
- It's like magic

00:00:54.443 --> 00:00:55.276
- Puppies

00:00:55.276 --> 00:00:57.194
- Cute animals, cute babies

00:00:57.194 --> 00:01:00.142
- It almost has to be a
goal, like playing cheek.

00:01:00.142 --> 00:01:01.984
What do you expect out of
a Super Bowl commercial,

00:01:01.984 --> 00:01:03.309
and kind of supert it.

00:01:03.309 --> 00:01:06.280
They all have some product truth in them.

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:09.156
It was the Volkswagen The Force commercial

00:01:09.156 --> 00:01:11.734
where the little kid
dressed up as Darth Vader

00:01:11.734 --> 00:01:14.537
and tried to make things
happen with his mind

00:01:14.537 --> 00:01:16.997
and he goes out and goes
like that to the car

00:01:16.997 --> 00:01:19.381
and the dad remote started
the car and the kid

00:01:19.381 --> 00:01:21.310
freaks out, it's really cute.

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:23.439
With a Volkswagen, it
does sort of feel like the

00:01:23.439 --> 00:01:25.951
force when you remote start a car.

00:01:25.951 --> 00:01:28.477
The Snickers Betty White commercial,

00:01:28.477 --> 00:01:29.938
that was a real classic one.

00:01:29.938 --> 00:01:33.281
They're like playing tackle football.

00:01:33.281 --> 00:01:34.352
- Better?

00:01:34.352 --> 00:01:36.489
- Snickers hunger does transform you into

00:01:36.489 --> 00:01:38.840
a different person.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:40.763
E-Trade is less about a product truth

00:01:40.763 --> 00:01:42.590
and more a media truth.

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:44.384
It's just a monkey dancing wearing

00:01:44.384 --> 00:01:47.652
an E-Trade shirt for
20 seconds and it says

00:01:47.652 --> 00:01:50.090
Well, we just wasted a million dollars.

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:51.734
How's your money?

00:01:51.734 --> 00:01:54.054
People watch the Super Bowl very aware

00:01:54.054 --> 00:01:56.094
of how much the commercials cost,

00:01:56.094 --> 00:01:58.388
and they think about whether that was

00:01:58.388 --> 00:01:59.782
worth that much money.

00:01:59.782 --> 00:02:02.156
So, it's tapping into what
people are already thinking.

00:02:02.156 --> 00:02:04.327
- I think the biggest
rule of the Super Bowl

00:02:04.327 --> 00:02:07.065
is there's no rules except what works.

00:02:07.065 --> 00:02:08.516
Surprising people is key.

00:02:08.516 --> 00:02:11.328
- (interviewer)Talk about your
current Super Bowl commercial.

00:02:11.328 --> 00:02:14.694
- We did the Avocados
from Mexico commercial.

00:02:14.694 --> 00:02:16.816
It's this perfect world.

00:02:16.816 --> 00:02:19.498
- You sealed the bad out
and kept the good in.

00:02:19.498 --> 00:02:21.623
- But, of course, they're just people so

00:02:21.623 --> 00:02:23.011
we're going to screw it up.

00:02:23.011 --> 00:02:23.844
- The chips are outside!

00:02:23.844 --> 00:02:24.737
(screams)

00:02:24.737 --> 00:02:26.900
There were hundreds of ideas pitched.

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:29.645
- Yeah, it just fluctuates
for months and months

00:02:29.645 --> 00:02:31.980
and months until finally
we wind up with that

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:34.294
one idea that made it through.

00:02:34.294 --> 00:02:36.440
- Using celebrities in
ways that are expected

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:39.233
I think is a really good
way to go at things.

00:02:39.233 --> 00:02:40.954
There were a SquareSpace one last year

00:02:40.954 --> 00:02:42.177
with John Malkovich.

00:02:42.177 --> 00:02:43.641
He was very upset because someone else

00:02:43.641 --> 00:02:45.594
had registered John Malkovich dot com,

00:02:45.594 --> 00:02:47.820
and it was just a super simple idea.

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:51.455
It kind of hinges a
little bit on star power

00:02:51.455 --> 00:02:53.434
and believability and scale.

00:02:53.434 --> 00:02:56.309
I was on a team that made
the Tourism Australia

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:58.529
commercial which involved pretending to

00:02:58.529 --> 00:03:00.598
make a movie called Dundee.

00:03:00.598 --> 00:03:02.236
- Ha ha, that's me

00:03:02.236 --> 00:03:04.149
- Brian Dundee?

00:03:04.149 --> 00:03:05.749
- Hollywood is kind of
rebooting every single

00:03:05.749 --> 00:03:07.054
movie from the eighties.

00:03:07.054 --> 00:03:08.973
Crocodile Dundee kind of stands out as one

00:03:08.973 --> 00:03:10.428
that hasn't been brought back.

00:03:10.428 --> 00:03:12.258
We wanted people to think that we were

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:13.777
actually making a real movie.

00:03:13.777 --> 00:03:16.543
Danny McBride is such an unlikely choice

00:03:16.543 --> 00:03:18.711
to play the son of Crocodile Dundee.

00:03:18.711 --> 00:03:19.823
Which is intentional.

00:03:19.823 --> 00:03:20.656
- You okay mate?

00:03:20.656 --> 00:03:21.752
- Nothing to see here man,

00:03:21.752 --> 00:03:23.734
just getting a clean
shave with my machete.

00:03:23.734 --> 00:03:25.895
- Really became the character on set.

00:03:25.895 --> 00:03:28.087
He was just constantly
riffing and improvising

00:03:28.087 --> 00:03:30.706
and doing the lines
better than we gave him.

00:03:30.706 --> 00:03:32.050
A lot of the moments that ended up in

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:33.987
the final cut were him riffing.

00:03:33.987 --> 00:03:35.801
- There's so much with Super Bowl spots.

00:03:35.801 --> 00:03:39.443
The process of making
one is kind of part of

00:03:39.443 --> 00:03:40.570
what makes it great.

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:43.701
I mean look at the success
that Doritos has had

00:03:43.701 --> 00:03:46.576
for years just kind of like crowdsourcing.

00:03:46.576 --> 00:03:48.081
(glass shatters)

00:03:48.081 --> 00:03:50.059
- For big visuals, like drop people in

00:03:50.059 --> 00:03:52.098
but you have to something
that ends up with

00:03:52.098 --> 00:03:54.460
some sort of substance and content.

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:56.596
- The key to making a
Super Bowl commercial

00:03:56.596 --> 00:03:58.674
is that if you haven't had fun making it

00:03:58.674 --> 00:04:00.620
people certainly aren't going
to have fun watching it.

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:01.453
- Totally.

00:04:01.453 --> 00:04:03.223
- (interviewer) Making a
Super Bowl commercial is

00:04:03.223 --> 00:04:05.295
kind of like making a diamond?

00:04:05.295 --> 00:04:07.008
- It's a really intense process.

00:04:07.008 --> 00:04:09.766
It's months and months of work.

00:04:09.766 --> 00:04:12.742
Because the prize is so
great it so stressful,

00:04:12.742 --> 00:04:16.365
but at the end you have
a beautiful diamond

00:04:16.365 --> 00:04:18.719
which is a commercial.

00:04:18.719 --> 00:04:21.302
(lively music)

